{"call_id":"call_96OviUyRM3nlSGLTJNySga1w","process_id":"45967","turn_id":"019ca680-ea9c-7db3-83cf-b867dcdf0135","command":["/bin/bash","-lc","kspec task get @01KJDQ17W --json"],"cwd":"/workspace","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"kspec task get @01KJDQ17W --json"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","stdout":"{\n  \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ17W53F5NN0CWTVSEY53R\",\n  \"slugs\": [],\n  \"title\": \"Ralph loop needs iteration-level timeout. When a spawned agent gets stuck (e.g., tool call hanging o\",\n  \"type\": \"task\",\n  \"description\": \"**What**: Ralph loop has no per-iteration timeout. When a spawned agent gets stuck (e.g., a tool call hanging on stdin, like the `kspec batch --commands \\\"\\\"` hang), ralph waits indefinitely. Claude Code's per-bash-command timeout (120s default) does not cover all hang scenarios — an agent can be alive but unresponsive at the ACP protocol level.\\n\\n**Where**:\\n- `src/cli/commands/ralph.ts` — main loop at line ~1127, the `agent.client.prompt()` call at line ~1373 and the reflection prompt call. These are the two main await points that can hang.\\n- `src/acp/client.ts` — the ACP client that manages the session/prompt lifecycle\\n\\n**How**:\\n- Add a configurable `--iteration-timeout <minutes>` CLI option (default: 20 minutes) to the ralph command registration (line ~868).\\n- Wrap the `agent.client.prompt()` calls in a `Promise.race` with a timeout. On timeout: (1) kill the stuck agent process via `agent.kill()`, (2) log the timeout as a failed iteration, (3) apply the existing retry/failure escalation logic.\\n- The timeout should cover the entire iteration (task-work prompt + optional reflection prompt), not individual prompts, since an iteration is the atomic unit of work.\\n- Consider using `AbortController` / `AbortSignal` if the ACP client supports it, otherwise use `Promise.race` with a timer.\\n\\n**Done when**:\\n- `kspec ralph --iteration-timeout 15` kills a stuck agent after 15 minutes and continues to the next iteration (or exits if max failures reached)\\n- Default timeout is 20 minutes\\n- Timeout events are logged to the session event store with type `iteration.timeout`\\n- Existing retry and failure escalation logic handles timeouts the same as other iteration failures\",\n  \"spec_ref\": \"@cli-ralph\",\n  \"status\": \"needs_work\",\n  \"blocked_by\": [],\n  \"closed_reason\": null,\n  \"depends_on\": [],\n  \"context\": [],\n  \"priority\": 3,\n  \"tags\": [],\n  \"vcs_refs\": [],\n  \"session_id\": null,\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:32:55.301Z\",\n  \"started_at\": \"2026-02-28T22:47:09.022Z\",\n  \"submitted_at\": \"2026-02-28T22:47:11.607Z\",\n  \"completed_at\": null,\n  \"notes\": [\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQW7RZ6DDS9BNKW8XMDXF4\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:47:39.935Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"Linked to @cli-ralph spec. New feature: iteration-level timeout for ralph loop. Spec covers ralph command.\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJK3T7PC2Z2H7RTVSQ8328M7\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T21:52:29.388Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"Implemented iteration-level timeout for ralph loop attempts. Added --iteration-timeout <minutes> (default 20), validated as positive numeric minutes, and applied timeout over full task-work+reflect attempt using Promise.race. On timeout, ralph now logs iteration.timeout events with iteration/attempt/timeout metadata, kills the stuck agent, and reuses existing retry/max-failure handling. Updated session event schema to include iteration.timeout and added regression tests in tests/ralph.test.ts for dry-run display, invalid value handling, and timeout event logging. Verification: npx vitest run tests/ralph.test.ts tests/sessions.test.ts (pass), npm test (pass). kspec validate still reports pre-existing project-level meta/reference/alignment/completeness issues unrelated to this change.\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJK3WXSEE5KSY4TDN2WYB5DG\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T21:53:57.550Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"Pushed commit f22d1109 to existing branch feat/session-stale-close-metadata (open PR #607: https://github.com/kynetic-ai/kynetic-spec/pull/607).\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJK48WZBHDXEHPAG6FTRW3T7\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T22:00:29.932Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 1] Review findings: MUST-FIX: PR #607 includes unrelated @core-skill-update changes in this task scope, and @cli-ralph AC coverage gate is incomplete (missing annotated coverage for ac-3, ac-4, ac-5, ac-14, ac-15, ac-17, ac-18).\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJK5TKC70952P6JSZXJC00ZM\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T22:27:38.504Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 2] Re-implemented iteration-level timeout for ralph with --iteration-timeout (default 20m), wrapping task-work+reflect prompts in Promise.race and emitting iteration.timeout events with iteration/attempt/timeout metadata before retry/failure handling. Added schema support for iteration.timeout in session event types. Closed AC coverage gaps by adding @cli-ralph AC annotations/tests for ac-3, ac-4, ac-5, ac-14, ac-15, ac-17, ac-18 and timeout behavior regression tests in tests/ralph.test.ts. Verification: npx vitest run tests/ralph.test.ts tests/sessions.test.ts (pass). kspec validate still reports pre-existing project-level schema/reference/alignment/completeness issues unrelated to this task.\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJK5VV3ECEA0AS7J74X8KMTN\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T22:28:19.182Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 2] Implemented and pushed iteration-timeout fix on branch feat/ralph-iteration-timeout. Commit: 3e730097. Opened PR #608: https://github.com/kynetic-ai/kynetic-spec/pull/608.\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJK608NF6GR4WB11X3BFQYAR\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T22:30:44.143Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"Automation status set to needs_review: Subagent completed but did not merge or kick back. Review required.\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJK60E21T7Y8DEVCNVY0WRQV\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T22:30:49.665Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"[RALPH SUBAGENT] Subagent completed but did not merge or kick back. Review required.\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJK6Y20KT1W73HHH9V2PCW4C\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T22:47:00.371Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"Reset from completed to pending\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJK6YR76FMMN3EJK160JAX6T\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T22:47:23.110Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 4] Review findings: MUST-FIX: Floating runIterationPrompts() promise causes unhandled rejection crash in Node.js 22 when iteration times out. disposeSpawnedAgent() closes the framing layer, rejecting the pending session/prompt request. The runIterationPrompts() Promise rejects with no catch handler, crashing the process before session.end and wrap-up agent run. Fix: store the Promise and attach .catch(() => {}) before the Promise.race. SHOULD-FIX: --iteration-timeout feature has no spec ACs in @cli-ralph; tests/ralph.test.ts lines 230 and 313 have no // AC: annotations. Add ACs to spec and annotate tests. Review posted at PR #608.\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJK704TWT5HRZ6R4VQ5Y7HZK\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T22:48:08.796Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"Automation status set to needs_review: Subagent timed out after 20 minutes\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJK707NECN9S8HRC3BHGVQ2A\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T22:48:11.694Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"[RALPH SUBAGENT] Subagent timed out after 20 minutes\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJK791KD9PKHACN3GH461C4V\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T22:53:00.397Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"FIX_CYCLE: 5 Addressed all review findings:\\n1. MUST-FIX: Fixed floating runIterationPrompts() promise by storing the promise in a variable and attaching .catch(() => {}) before Promise.race — prevents unhandled rejection crash in Node.js 22 when timeout fires first and disposeSpawnedAgent() rejects the pending prompt.\\n2. SHOULD-FIX: Added spec ACs ac-24/ac-25/ac-26 to @cli-ralph for --iteration-timeout feature (default behavior, validation, timeout event logging).\\n3. SHOULD-FIX: Added // AC: @cli-ralph annotations to tests at lines 230 (ac-25), 313 (ac-24, ac-26), and 222 (ac-24).\\nAll 140 ralph tests pass. Opening new PR for these fixes on a separate branch.\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJK7AYYW3N608J9D0FH4B2DE\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T22:54:03.228Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"FIX_CYCLE: 5 complete. Opened PR #610 (https://github.com/kynetic-ai/kynetic-spec/pull/610) with:\\n1. Fixed floating runIterationPrompts() promise (.catch(() => {}) before Promise.race)\\n2. Added @cli-ralph ac-24/ac-25/ac-26 for --iteration-timeout feature\\n3. Added // AC: annotations to tests/ralph.test.ts\\nAll 140 ralph tests pass.\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    }\n  ],\n  \"todos\": [],\n  \"automation\": \"needs_review\",\n  \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"\n}\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ17W53F5NN0CWTVSEY53R\",\n  \"slugs\": [],\n  \"title\": \"Ralph loop needs iteration-level timeout. When a spawned agent gets stuck (e.g., tool call hanging o\",\n  \"type\": \"task\",\n  \"description\": \"**What**: Ralph loop has no per-iteration timeout. When a spawned agent gets stuck (e.g., a tool call hanging on stdin, like the `kspec batch --commands \\\"\\\"` hang), ralph waits indefinitely. Claude Code's per-bash-command timeout (120s default) does not cover all hang scenarios — an agent can be alive but unresponsive at the ACP protocol level.\\n\\n**Where**:\\n- `src/cli/commands/ralph.ts` — main loop at line ~1127, the `agent.client.prompt()` call at line ~1373 and the reflection prompt call. These are the two main await points that can hang.\\n- `src/acp/client.ts` — the ACP client that manages the session/prompt lifecycle\\n\\n**How**:\\n- Add a configurable `--iteration-timeout <minutes>` CLI option (default: 20 minutes) to the ralph command registration (line ~868).\\n- Wrap the `agent.client.prompt()` calls in a `Promise.race` with a timeout. On timeout: (1) kill the stuck agent process via `agent.kill()`, (2) log the timeout as a failed iteration, (3) apply the existing retry/failure escalation logic.\\n- The timeout should cover the entire iteration (task-work prompt + optional reflection prompt), not individual prompts, since an iteration is the atomic unit of work.\\n- Consider using `AbortController` / `AbortSignal` if the ACP client supports it, otherwise use `Promise.race` with a timer.\\n\\n**Done when**:\\n- `kspec ralph --iteration-timeout 15` kills a stuck agent after 15 minutes and continues